{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the appworker account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"appworker was initially absent, then created as UID/GID 1001 with a home directory and login shell, and remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f441135969f4545","cmd-22f52c5d73454172","cmd-e9eb88c102674581"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Set appworker login sessions to an open-files limit of 8,192.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The PAM limits policy sets both soft and hard nofile limits to 8192. A PAM-backed runuser login directly observed 8192/8192 before restart and again after recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a8883b918d1b41ac","cmd-56580ee9b9164009","cmd-ad7fbf7280214812","cmd-e9eb88c102674581"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Set appworker login sessions to a process limit of 256.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy sets both soft and hard nproc limits to 256. A PAM-backed runuser login directly observed 256/256 before restart and again after recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a8883b918d1b41ac","cmd-56580ee9b9164009","cmd-ad7fbf7280214812","cmd-e9eb88c102674581"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary managed-system mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. Account creation, creation of the previously absent limits.d directory, and policy installation directly supported the task; the reboot scheduling supported the mandatory restart protocol. The failed initial policy write did not create a file. Afterward there were no failed services or package-database errors, while socket and temporary-file differences were ordinary boot-identity/PID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-22f52c5d73454172","cmd-670e9bc034b04c0e","cmd-ee58efe3906048da","cmd-a8883b918d1b41ac","cmd-eb11a1ca5f184e4d","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide node1 restart protocol is also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged the scheduled restart, observed a changed boot identity, and directly verified recovered system services, account data, policy, and effective limits. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["Effective behavior was directly exercised through `runuser --login`, not an interactive console or SSH login. The earlier `su -` probe showed default limits because that distinct Arch Linux PAM service did not include pam_limits; therefore the behavioral evidence does not cover every conceivable user-switching/session-opening service (cmd-0b7332bacb214c04, cmd-35718e35fac94140, cmd-56580ee9b9164009)."]}
